      "role": "ally",
      "pronouns": "he/him",
      "armor": "",
      "agenda": "",
      "agendaKind": "",
      "notes": "Herald of Gorse, halfling, sixty, of enormous and unshakeable dignity. He has read the prophecy aloud in every town square in the kingdom and has never once been in on a joke. He identifies the player as the stranger in the hat and thereafter regards the player as an official matter. He travels with the party as far as he can be persuaded, which is quite far.",
      "secret": "He chose the player not for the hat but because the player was the only person in the square who did not run when he said the word prophecy; he considers this the bravest thing he has seen in forty years of heralding.",
