  "locations": [
    {
      "name": "Little Piddle-on-the-Marsh",
      "description": "A marsh town of reed roofs, duckboards and competitive vegetable growing, where the Annual Marrow matters more than the crown and the crown knows it. The herald reads the prophecy from the pump. The Royal Postal Griffin lands on the green, twice daily, and does not carry passengers."
    },
    {
      "name": "Mildew Hall",
      "description": "A haunted mansion on the road to the Wood: damp, grand, genuinely eerie, and occupied by the Mildew Hall Players, a company of the dead who died of nothing in particular and took up theatre. Every haunting is a rehearsal. The props cupboard holds the Lantern of Mild Suspicion. The only agreed map of the Wood That Disagrees is in the director's desk."
    },
    {
      "name": "The Wood That Disagrees",
      "description": "An ancient forest whose trees argue about which way is north and rearrange the paths to make their point. Keith's bridge crosses the river at its middle; Doris the basilisk squints through its eastern half; Ambrose the unicorn keeps a clearing nobody has ever been pure enough to enter; Dunmore the gnome optician lives in a stump because nobody else will have him."
    },
    {
      "name": "Great Snoring",
      "description": "A town of sheep, orchards and a monastery whose monks have not spoken in a decade and communicate by eyebrow. The calendar bell hangs unrung, so nobody in Gorse knows what day it is. The Oracle of Gorse sleeps in the orchard with her cat."
    },
    {
      "name": "Hobb's End",
      "description": "The arena town at the foot of Mount Considerable, entirely organised around the Rescue Trials, held whenever a princess is taken, and cheese, held constantly. The Trials have been non-lethal by tradition since the incident nobody discusses."
    },
    {
      "name": "The Trials Arena",
      "description": "Hobb's End's arena: a ring of turf and cheerful bunting where the Hydra Committee is kept in a paddock with a suggestion box and Sir Wendel the Undefeated enters slowly to enormous applause. The rule is that nobody's feelings are hurt. The prize is the Sword of Reasonable Doubt."
    },
    {
      "name": "Mount Considerable",
      "description": "A mountain of no particular importance, well kept because the dragon keeps it, with signs that apologise for the gradient and a mat at the cave mouth. Inside: a tidy hoard, a reading chair, three volumes of memoir, a princess with a crossword, and Grunwald."
    }
  ],
  "creatures": [
